    {
      "text": "I sat down at the kitchen table and jotted out a list. A can of lubricant spray, new hinges just in case, a handful of screws and the right size screwdriver. I also needed some pine boardsand  metal brackets for the shelf I'd been meaning to build in the garage. With that list tucked in my wallet, I headed to the hardware store. There's something about walking into that place that always gets me pumped. The smell of wood, the rows of tools, it just puts me in a good mood. I wandered down the aisles, checked off each item, and even asked a guy in an apron if the hinges I'd picked were strong enough. He nodded and handed me a box of self-tapping screws with a grin. Loading everything into the trunk, I felt a mix of anticipation and contentment. I liked the idea of fixing and building things myself. It's not just about the hinge and the shelf. It's about taking care of my space and proving to myself that I can sort out these little problems. Back at home, as I unpacked the supplies, I felt ready to get to work and pretty proudthat  I had set myself up to make it happen.",
